## Backend (`convex/`)

Key files:
- `schema.ts`: tables/indexes (`images`, `profiles`, `importBatches`, boards/decks/storyboards, etc.)
- `images/`: image domain split. [`index.ts`](convex/images/index.ts) re-exports public `api.images.*`; cross-module **internal** calls use the `internalApi.images.*` shim in [`shared.ts`](convex/images/shared.ts) (maps nested `images/analysis`, `images/ingest`, …). Modules: `library.ts`, `ingest.ts`, `moderation.ts`, `lifecycle.ts`, `uploads.ts`, `analysis.ts`, `generation.ts`, `shared.ts`. Orchestration lease mutations live in [`orchestrationState.ts`](convex/orchestrationState.ts), not `analysis.ts`.
- `orchestrationSeam.ts` / `orchestrationCore.ts` / `triggerDispatch.ts` / `orchestration.ts`: Trigger HTTP seam, Node idempotency/status helpers, SDK dispatch, protected callbacks.
- `mediaAdapter.ts` + `lib/mediaAdapter.ts` + `mediaStorage.ts`: canonical storage paths / public URLs vs Node upload/cleanup actions.
- `vision.ts`: analysis + variation generation flow and prompt planning
- `colorExtraction.ts` + `colorExtractionUrls.ts` + `colorExtractionAdmin.ts` / `colorExtractionWrite.ts`: dominant image swatches (`images.colors`) via sharp + [colorPaletteCore](mdc:src/lib/colorPaletteCore.ts); admin mutations require auth (`reExtractAll` / `reExtractForImage`)
- `discordNotifications.ts`: webhook status events to Discord channel
- `http.ts`: public HTTP routes (`/ingestExternal`, `/discordQueue`, `/discordModerate`, `/smartAnalyzeImage`, `/orchestration/*`)
- `decks.ts`, `storyboards.ts`: output/organization features; **`decks.update`** persists composer edits (blocks, palette, slides, FX)

Important image fields:
- `status`: `pending` / `draft` / `active`
- `aiStatus`: `queued` / `processing` / `completed` / `failed`
- `sourceType`: `upload` / `discord` / `pinterest` / `ai`
- `sref`, `tags`, `colors`, `group`, `projectName`, `parentImageId`

## Frontend (`src/`)

Key files:
- `App.tsx`: auth, Convex subscriptions, tweaks, keyboard shortcuts, view bodies
- `components/shell/`: **Topbar**, **Sidebar**, `useAppView` / `useLibraryFilterState` / `useTableColumnVisibility`, view ids / table-column types (`types.ts`)
- `components/pd/GalleryView.tsx`: library gallery (random / project rows), like + save-to-board
- `components/pd/TableView.tsx`: library table (sort, selection, metadata/palette refresh)
- `components/pd/ImageDetailDrawer.tsx`: image details, edit metadata, variations, lineage
- `components/ImageUploadForm.tsx`: local upload + Discord queue review/approve/discard
- `lib/colorExtraction.ts`: frontend color extraction helper

## Discord Bot (`services/discord-bot/`)

Key file:
- `src/index.js`

Capabilities:
- Slash commands for presets and ingest workflows.
- Queue review and moderation commands/buttons.
- Reaction-triggered ingest from channel messages and RSS-forwarded posts.
- Auto variation-control buttons on approved status messages.
- Talks to Convex HTTP endpoints with API key auth.

Runtime model:
- Separate long-running process (not hosted by Vercel frontend).

## Scripts

Common scripts:
- `bun run dev:frontend`
- `bun run dev:backend` (avoid when targeting production data)
- `bun run build` (frontend build)
- `bun run deploy:convex`
- `bun run discord:bot`

## Current Conventions

- Keep production Convex usage explicit; avoid accidental `convex dev` when working on prod.
- For Discord ingest/moderation updates, update both:
  - Convex HTTP/backend behavior
  - `services/discord-bot/src/index.js`
- Keep lineage consistent:
  - generated images must keep `parentImageId`
  - Discord lineage keeps `sref` from parent/root
- Prefer manual approval queue for Discord-ingested content before expensive AI steps.
